<common-name datatype='string'>putative ethanolamine catabolic microcompartment shell protein EutS</common-name>
<comment datatype='string'>The crystal structure of EutS has been determined at 1.65 &amp;Aring; resolution.  The &amp;alpha;/&amp;beta; structure resembles that of carboxysomal shell proteins, although the cyclic hexameric structure has a bend of approximately 40&amp;deg;.  This may allow formation of the edges of a polyhedral microcompartment shell [&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/20044574&quot;&gt;Tanaka10a&lt;/a&gt;].
&lt;p&gt;
A G39V mutant protein forms a flat, symmetric hexameric structure [&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/20044574&quot;&gt;Tanaka10a&lt;/a&gt;].
&lt;p&gt;
The functions of the orthologous &lt;i&gt;eut&lt;/i&gt; operon genes for ethanolamine utilization in &lt;i&gt;Salmonella enterica&lt;/i&gt; have been studied experimentally [&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/10464203&quot;&gt;Kofoid99&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/16585748&quot;&gt;Penrod06&lt;/a&gt;].</comment>
